          "id": "p3-4",
          "speaker": "Jake",
          "text": "Are they hard to control?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-5",
          "speaker": "Clare",
          "text": "Well, I don’t have discipline problems as such. It’s just that they don’t seem to think that science has anything to do with their lives. It’s depressing. They listen to what I say, and I gave them a test last week and the results weren’t too bad, but there’s no real engagement."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-6",
          "speaker": "Jake",
          "text": "Right."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-7",
          "speaker": "Clare",
          "text": "And as part of my teaching practice, I have to design an experiment for them to do. I was wondering about something on the children’s diets… you know, asking them to record what they eat and maybe linking it to their state of health."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-8",
          "speaker": "Jake",
          "text": "Mmm. Let’s think. So your methodology would involve the children recording what they eat. OK, but you’d also need to have access to the children’s medical records and I don’t think people would be happy about that; confidentiality would be an issue. If you could get the right data, the conclusions might be significant, but I suspect it’s just not going to be easy."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-9",
          "speaker": "Clare",
          "text": "Right."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-10",
          "speaker": "Jake",
          "text": "Have you thought about doing an experiment using animals?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-11",
          "speaker": "Clare",
          "text": "Wouldn’t that be upsetting for the children?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-12",
          "speaker": "Jake",
          "text": "Well, the animals don’t have to be harmed in any way. It could just be an experiment where they’re given a certain diet and the effects are observed."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-13",
          "speaker": "Clare",
          "text": "Would I have to get permission to use animals?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-14",
          "speaker": "Jake",
          "text": "Yes, you’d have to submit an outline of the experiment and fill in a form, but it’s quite straightforward."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-15",
          "speaker": "Clare",
          "text": "But if we found out that, say, a particular diet affects the health of animals, the same thing wouldn’t necessarily be true for people, would it?"
