          "id": "p3-20",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "Well, they aren’t decorative, are they, like other objects. Plus, nowadays, people don’t keep them out on shelves as much as they used to."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-21",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "That’s such a pity. When I visit someone - if they have, say, a colorful book on a table, it’s the first thing I’m drawn to."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-22",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "I agree-and book covers can be a work of art in themselves. Some are really eye-catching."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-23",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "I’ve always been taught to handle books carefully. If you watch someone take a book off a shelf, well, they usually do it wrong."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-24",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "Ah, my grandfather says, you should put your hand right over the top of the book . . . or if you can’t do that, pull the other books on the shelf aside so that you can hold the whole cover."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-25",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "When did you learn all this?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-26",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "He watched me pull a heavy book off the shelf when I was small, and it fell on the floor and broke apart."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-27",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "Oh dear!"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-28",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "I can still remember it!"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-29",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "You know what I really like?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-30",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "What?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-31",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "The smell of new books."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-32",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "Me too."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-33",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "My parents used to laugh at me when I was a kid because I loved putting books up to my nose. Almost as much as reading them!"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-34",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "New books aren’t cheap, though, are they?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-35",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "I guess we’re lucky we can buy them."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-36",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "My grandfather stocks second-hand books as well as new ones and they don’t smell quite as good. …………………………………………………………………………………………………………….."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-37",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "I’d love to have a bookshop like your grandfather. What’s it like?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-38",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "Well, it’s quite big - it’s got two floors and an attic, and he stocks all kinds of books really."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-39",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "I guess he treasures things like first editions and other rare books."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-40",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "Yeah - you might think he’d keep those in the attic or somewhere."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-41",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": ". . . so they’d be hidden?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-42",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "Yeah. But he likes people to know that he has them. So, he puts them out in the shop but makes sure you need a ladder to get them."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-43",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "Right. That would prevent any thefts!"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-44",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "Uhuh."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-45",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "Does he stock books for children?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-46",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "He does. He particularly likes to encourage kids to read; he always says that he used to sit under the stairs as a child with a pile of books and read them all."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-47",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "Is that where he keeps them, then?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-48",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "Not exactly- he’s got a dedicated area on the ground floor with cushions so that parents can enter with their toddlers, go there and spend some time reading to them."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-49",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "Oh cool."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-50",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "And then there’s a place for pushchairs by the front door. And a café if anyone needs refreshments."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-51",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "That’s good to know."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-52",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "As I said, it’s a big shop and there’s a storage area out the back as well."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-53",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "Oh, what does he keep there? Books he wants to throw away?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-54",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "He hardly ever throws anything away -he just leaves unwanted books by the front door for customers to take."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-55",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "Well, that’s very nice."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-56",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "Yeah-and books people or institutions have requested, they all go at the far end."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-57",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "Oh."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-58",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "He thinks it’s best to keep these out of the main shopping area as they’re boxed and new."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-59",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "Did you get your coursebooks from him?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-60",
          "speaker": "Jane",
          "text": "Naturally. He stocks books for a lot of the colleges. He used to keep these books on the first floor, but now there’s a new university in my hometown, he’s moved them downstairs to attract the students. They’re actually part of the coffee shop, on low shelves all around it."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-61",
          "speaker": "Kieran",
          "text": "Pretty central then. You’ll have to take me there some time!"
        }
      ]
